          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What standards do your disposal processes follow?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS adheres to NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2 media sanitization guidelines and DoD 5220.22-M destruction protocols. We maintain documented procedures supporting HIPAA, FACTA, and GLBA compliance for financial and healthcare clients in Bakersfield and Kern County."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is business pickup service free in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, STS provides complimentary pickup across Bakersfield and Kern County for qualifying commercial volumes of IT equipment, servers, and computers. Contact our team to confirm lot qualification and schedule collection."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do you handle California universal waste compliance?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Our workflows align fully with California Department of Toxic Substances Control (DTSC) regulations and CalRecycle universal waste rules, ensuring all non-reusable materials avoid landfills through environmentally sustainable processing."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does it take to schedule a pickup in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most Bakersfield commercial pickups are scheduled within 3 to 5 business days of your request. We coordinate flexible logistics to prevent disruption to daily operations at corporate, clinical, and industrial facilities."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications and credentials govern your processing?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment collected in Bakersfield is staged locally and processed at STS certified processing facilities in Jacksonville and Houston, Texas, adhering to strict environmental, chain-of-custody, and data sanitization standards."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do you support HIPAA compliance for Kern County healthcare providers?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We provide physical hard drive shredding and cryptographic data sanitization under HIPAA 45 CFR §164.312 requirements, issuing serialized Certificates of Destruction for medical networks like Kern Medical and Adventist Health Bakersfield."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Where does Bakersfield electronic waste go after pickup?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Collected hardware is inventoried, secured, and routed to an STS processing operation for sanitization and material recovery. No toxic components or e-waste materials are deposited into local Kern County landfills."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can Bakersfield businesses recover value from surplus IT assets?",
